        'A set of washable cloths, by contrast, represents a single purchase that, with normal laundering, lasts for years of regular use. Framed in relative terms, the total spend on paper towels over even a single year typically exceeds the one-time cost of a comparable set of reusable cloths, meaning the switch effectively pays for itself well within that first year, often within just the first few months for a household that uses paper towels heavily.',
